    "durationMs": 238125,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete. All tests passed:\n\n**What I built** — an ASP.NET Core 8 minimal API in `/workspace` using EF Core + Npgsql as the persistence layer:\n\n- `POST /links` — validates the body by parsing it manually, so malformed JSON, invalid/missing `url`, and invalid codes all return 422 JSON with an `error` field; duplicate custom codes return 409; generated codes are 8 chars from `[a-z0-9]` with unique-index-backed collision retry. Returns 201 with `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}`, URL stored unchanged (only trimmed).\n- `GET /links/{code}` — 200 or 404 JSON error.\n- `GET /r/{code}` — atomic `ExecuteUpdateAsync` click increment (exactly once per request), then 302 with `Location`.\n- `GET /links` — `{items, total}` ordered by ascending `Id`.\n- `DATABASE_URL` (PostgreSQL URL) is parsed into an Npgsql connection string at runtime — no hard-coded credentials.\n\n**Infrastructure** — EF Core migration `InitialCreate` (Links table, unique code index), `start.sh` that runs `dotnet ef database update` then serves the built app in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (app startup also applies pending migrations as a safety net with retry), and a README with start instructions.\n\n**Verified live against Postgres**: every status code and error shape above, 20-char/4-char code boundaries, `code: null`, POST without Content-Type header, and a full restart cycle — clicks (2 → 3) and all links survived the restart, with the second run confirming \"database is already up to date\". The test server has been stopped."
